cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Implementation-Risk Differentials in Hydrogen Technology Pathways:
  Evidence from a Segmented Investment Ecosystem and
  Carbon-Price-Conditional Risk
message: >-
  If you use this software or replication package, please cite the
  associated working paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sake
    family-names: Saakstra
    email: s.saakstra@vu.nl
    affiliation: Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam --- Department of Econometrics
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sakesaakstra/blueCCS-hydrogen'
abstract: >-
  Replication package for Saakstra (2026). The repository contains the
  full computational pipeline (Python + R) for an eleven-estimator
  robustness battery analysing the determinants of hydrogen project
  cancellation, with a focus on the carbon-price-conditional hazard
  differential between Blue_CCS and PEM technologies. Includes data
  ingestion, panel construction, propensity-based corrections, Fine-Gray
  competing-risks decomposition, shared-frailty Cox estimation,
  delta-method marginal effects, and leave-one-region-out robustness
  checks.
keywords:
  - hydrogen
  - carbon capture
  - project cancellation
  - transition risk
  - Fine-Gray competing risks
  - marginal effects
  - propensity score
  - doubly robust estimation
  - entropy balancing
  - carbon-price-conditional risk
